### ============================================================================
### CodeCraftHub - every endpoint as a runnable request.
###
### How to use:
###   1. Start the app:  mvn spring-boot:run
###   2. Open this file in IntelliJ IDEA (built-in HTTP client) or in VS Code
###      with the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above any
###      request. The requests are ordered so you can run them top to bottom.
###
### Prefer the command line? The README has the equivalent curl command for each
### of these requests.
### ============================================================================

@host = http://localhost:8080


### 1. List courses - empty the very first time
GET {{host}}/api/courses


### 2. Create a course (status omitted -> defaults to "Not Started")
# @name createPython
POST {{host}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Python Basics",
  "description": "Learn Python fundamentals",
  "target_date": "2026-12-31"
}


### 3. Create a second course, already in progress
# @name createSpring
POST {{host}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Spring Boot Basics",
  "description": "Learn to build REST APIs with Spring Boot",
  "target_date": "2026-11-30",
  "status": "In Progress"
}


### 4. Create a third course that is already finished
POST {{host}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Git and GitHub",
  "description": "Version control in practice",
  "target_date": "2026-10-01",
  "status": "Completed"
}


### 5. Read one course by id (try the id returned by request 2)
GET {{host}}/api/courses/1


### 6. List only the courses in progress
GET {{host}}/api/courses?status=In Progress


### 7. Search in name and description (case-insensitive)
GET {{host}}/api/courses/search?q=spring


### 8. Search with a status filter as well
GET {{host}}/api/courses/search?q=&status=Completed


### 9. Statistics for the whole learning plan
GET {{host}}/api/courses/stats


### 10. Update a course: PUT replaces the editable fields
PUT {{host}}/api/courses/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Python Basics",
  "description": "Halfway through - now doing the exercises",
  "target_date": "2027-01-31",
  "status": "In Progress"
}


### 11. Delete a course -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{host}}/api/courses/3


### ============================================================================
### Error cases - these are supposed to fail, that is the point.
### ============================================================================

### 12. Unknown id -> 404 with a JSON error body
GET {{host}}/api/courses/9999


### 13. Id that is not a number -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/courses/abc


### 14. Missing and blank required fields -> 400 with field_errors
POST {{host}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "target_date": null
}


### 15. Status that does not exist -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mystery Course",
  "target_date": "2026-12-31",
  "status": "Finished"
}


### 16. Unknown status used as a filter -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/courses?status=Finished


### 17. Body that is not valid JSON -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "broken"


### 18. Wrong date format -> 400 (expected: yyyy-MM-dd)
POST {{host}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Wrong Date Course",
  "target_date": "31/12/2026"
}
